_thumb/scy64w.jpg"}, {"id": 1594252, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scy64s.jpg"}, {"id": 1594253, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scy64t.jpg"}], "slug": "car-and-driver", "summary": "\"Car and Driver\" is a 1992 racing game that was developed by Lerner Research and published by Electronic Arts. The developer, Lerner Research, merged with Blue Sky Productions, to form Looking Glass Technologies, later renamed Looking Glass Studios.\n\nThe game was designed to look and feel like the pages of the \"Car and Driver\" magazine, and it featured detailed reviews and statistics for each of the 10 playable cars. These cars included the Porsche 959, Ferrari F40, and Lamborghini Countach, among others. The game included 10 tracks, some of which were based on famous driving routes. Notably, the game was praised for its physics model, realism and controls.", "themes": [{"id": 32, "name": "Non-fiction"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/car-and-driver", "videos": [{"id": 157243, "name": "Gameplay Video", "video_id": "uXI1deYzLFo", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uXI1deYzLFo", "title": "Car and Driver gameplay (PC Game, 1992)", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uXI1deYzLFo/maxresdefault.jpg"}]}